{"groups":[{"members":["c1","c2"],"primary":"c1","title":"Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance (RSO) allowable annual rent increase","requirement":"Rent on RSO-covered units may be increased only once every 12 months, by no more than the annual allowable percentage published by LAHD. From February 2, 2026, landlords may no longer add a utilities percentage or an extra 10% for an added dependent; a 10% increase is still allowed for an additional non-dependent tenant, and rent may reset to market rate after certain vacancies.","key_value":"One increase per 12 months, capped at the LAHD annual allowable percentage (3% for July 1, 2025 - June 30, 2026; the figure for the period from July 1, 2026 is not stated in these sources); no added utilities or dependent percentage from 2026-02-02; +10% for an additional non-dependent tenant","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"L.A.M.C. § 151.00 et seq. (Los Angeles Rent Stabilization Ordinance)","coverage_conditions":"Rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978, plus replacement units under LAMC § 151.28. Covered types: apartments, condominiums, townhomes, duplexes, two or more single-family dwellings on the same parcel, hotel/motel/rooming-house/boarding-house rooms occupied by the same tenant for more than 30 consecutive days, residential units attached to a commercial building, ADUs, JADUs, and mobile homes and recreational vehicles in mobile home parks.","exemptions":"Rent amount is not regulated for condominium and townhome tenancies that commenced after December 31, 1995. A Luxury Exemption is available if the landlord can establish the monthly rent charged on or before May 31, 1978. The source mentions temporary exemptions but does not detail them.","coverage_from":"c1","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[{"id":"c3","reason":"The record contains no rent-increase rule. It only refers to the RSO in the context of an eviction filing requirement (the Landlord Declaration), which belongs to the eviction category, and it has no cap, coverage or exemption content."}]}
